package dev.sidebike.app.ui.theme

import androidx.compose.material3.darkColorScheme
import androidx.compose.material3.lightColorScheme

/**
 * Material 3 color roles.
 *
 * Design decision (documented in `docs/design/01-ui-spec.md`):
 * - The static fallback is the MD3 **baseline** color scheme. It is generated by the Material 3
 *   `lightColorScheme()` / `darkColorScheme()` factories, i.e. every value is a real MD3 color
 *   role token with verified contrast — this file is the only place in the app allowed to own
 *   color decisions.
 * - On Android 12+ (API 31) the theme upgrades to **dynamic color** derived from the system
 *   wallpaper, so the app follows the user's Material You palette automatically.
 * - UI code must never hard-code colors; it consumes `MaterialTheme.colorScheme.*` roles only.
 */
internal val SidebikeLightColors = lightColorScheme()
internal val SidebikeDarkColors = darkColorScheme()
